// state-flow-1 and state-flow-project-1 are in their own part files. Options at their defaults (oracleAnalyzer false,
// entryPoint "all", sourceProvided true, returnKindsHex as given); here only the matchers read them, verbatim.
// Source: gate/data-layer/packs/data-layer/candidates/rules/data-layer-serverplan-state-tripwires.json.
//
// The 28 clauses have one shape: one input `events` and the same final query (dedupe on (__path, line, scope, terminal
// [, detail]), first by (__start, __end)). Their stage relations carry the clause id as a column in place of a per-clause
// name prefix. Each clause is per file (partitionBy file). An `events` row is the matched node (ROOT is the node itself).
// Optional captures, read by exact tree relations: SCOPE (`inside` a function_definition, stopBy function_definition) is
// the node's nearest strict function_definition ancestor (`nearest`); TERM (the same `any` in all 28 matchers) is the
// call's `function` identifier or that attribute's `attribute`, a class/function definition's `name`, or an attribute's
// `attribute`. The detail captures IR, IR_NAME, FIELD are required in their matchers and exported by the atom
// (executor-ir-dispatch's `each: IR_NAME`: one row per IR_NAME binding).
//
// Builtins: @line (new: the 1-based line of a node's first byte, W's `startLine` and the syntax table's `line`),
// @printf. A builtin with no value (SQL NULL) binds nothing.
// requireNonemptyInput (events): an empty input gives no rows here.
// ties: row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY __path, line, scope, terminal[, detail] ORDER BY __start, __end) = 1 keeps every
// node of the least (__start, __end); distinct nodes with one span are all kept.
// findings layer (§8): the final query's column renames (path, start_byte, end_byte) and coalesce(…, '') output
// columns; the finding key here is "line|scope|terminal|detail" with '' for NULL.
